course: dictionary
lesson: 4001
title: Old spellings and jail
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Gaol is an old British spelling of jail. The two words sound exactly the same and mean the same thing: a prison where people are locked up. You will see gaol in old books and on old buildings. «Old Melbourne Gaol» is a famous old prison in Australia.
explain: Gaol can also be a verb, meaning to put someone in prison. Look at the clues around it. In «Toad is sent to gaol for twenty years», the words sent and twenty years tell you that gaol is a place where a person is kept for a long time, not a cage or a village.
explain: Some words join gaol to other words. «Gaol-birds» are people who have often been in prison. The Rat says Toad «keeps company with gaol-birds», so the clue is company: Toad is friends with people who have been in prison. A good check is to swap in jail and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Gaol means a prison, the same as jail. Only the spelling is old.
fact: Gaol is also a verb: to gaol someone means to put them in prison.
fact: A gaol-bird is someone who has often been in prison.
fact: Long ago people were locked in the stocks, and some castles were really used as gaols.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, Toad is sent to gaol for twenty years, then escapes disguised as a washerwoman.
exercise: «Old Melbourne Gaol» is a famous old prison in Australia. What does gaol mean? | A shop that sells sweets | A kind of boat | A small village on a hill | *A prison
exercise: «Toad is sent to gaol for twenty years.» What does gaol mean here? | A long train journey | *A prison | A new school | A kind of hat
exercise: «Does Toad think the Rat enjoys hearing that he keeps company with gaol-birds?» What is a gaol-bird? | A farmer who keeps hens | *Someone who has often been in prison | A bird that sings at dawn | A bird that lives in a cage
test: The police will gaol the thief if they catch him. What does gaol mean in this sentence? | To run away very fast | *To put someone in prison | To find a lost dog | To go shopping for food
test: Gaol is an old British spelling of which word? | Gall | Gale | *Jail | Goal
exam: Which word means the same as gaol? | Garden | *Jail | Gallop | Gravy
